Intelligence Gaps
Unconfirmed whether 4688 command-line auditing is enabled on EPA Windows hosts. If the GPO is off, Splunk cannot match the redirect signature and Splunk coverage collapses to process-name lineage only. Verify: index=epa_* EventCode=4688 Process_Command_Line=* | stats count by index
MDE sensor coverage is unknown. Hosts not onboarded (legacy servers, domain controllers, appliances) are invisible to Defender — and these are frequent lateral-movement targets. Splunk WinEventLog may cover some of these; confirm overlap.
wmiexec.py -nooutput mode drops the redirect entirely: no ADMIN$\__ in the command line and no file written to C:\Windows. Both the command-line signature and the file-create signal miss it; only the WmiPrvSE.exe -> cmd.exe lineage query catches this variant.
No Sysmon means no EventCode 1 and reliance on 4688, which is noisier and GPO-dependent. Consider Sysmon deployment as a follow-on recommendation.
Defender AH 30-day retention limits historical look-back; older activity is only visible in Splunk if retained and command lines are present.


Notes
The __<epoch> filename is time.time() from the operator's host at command send-time. Extract it (redirect_epoch) and sort ascending to reconstruct the session as a keystroke transcript, independent of sensor timestamps.
Secondary signal: the output file lands in C:\Windows as __<number> and is deleted immediately after the read. A file-create rule on C:\Windows\__<digits> catches sessions even when the command line is obfuscated.
Default UNC host is 127.0.0.1 but is operator-configurable — do not pin the hunt to loopback. The /Q /c + ADMIN$\__ pair is the durable anchor.
Expected false-positive rate is near zero: legitimate software does not redirect output to \\...\ADMIN$\__<number>. Both KQL and SPL queries are promotable to detections largely unchanged if the hunt validates.
Existing coverage gap: the ESCU rule "PowerShell Invoke WmiExec Usage" keys on the string invoke-wmiexec in 4104 script-block logs — that catches the PowerShell Invoke-TheHash tool, not Impacket wmiexec.py. This hunt covers the Impacket behavioral pattern the rule cannot see.


